<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">8 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 8 February, from 1238 to 1974.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mongols" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mongols.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1238">1238 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">788 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mongols sack Vladimir in north-eastern Rus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batu-khan">Batu Khan</a>'s army stormed and burned Vladimir, the capital of the leading Russian principality. The Mongol conquest brought the Russian lands under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> for some two centuries.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1347">1347 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">679 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Byzantine civil war ends in a power-sharing agreement</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The civil war fought over the guardianship of the young John V Palaiologos, between the regency of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anna-of-savoy">Anna of Savoy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-vi-kantakouzenos">John VI Kantakouzenos</a>, ended in a power-sharing agreement. Kantakouzenos then reigned as emperor until 1354.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-vi-kantakouzenos">John VI Kantakouzenos</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1587">1587 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">439 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mary, Queen of Scots is executed at Fotheringhay</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After nineteen years in English captivity, Mary was beheaded for plotting against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a>. Her execution removed the Catholic claimant to the English throne and helped provoke the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Spanish Armada</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-england">Kingdom of England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Spanish Armada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1693">1693 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">333 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Royal charter founds the College of William and Mary</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">William III and Mary II granted a charter for a college in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, later sited at Williamsburg. It is the second-oldest college in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson">Thomas Jefferson</a> studied there.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1865">1865 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">161 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Delaware rejects the Thirteenth Amendment</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delaware's legislature voted against the amendment abolishing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>, although the state had remained in the Union. It ratified the amendment only symbolically, in 1901.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1904">1904 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">122 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Japan attacks the Russian fleet at Port Arthur</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Japanese torpedo boats struck the Russian Pacific squadron at night, opening the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war">Russo-Japanese War</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s victory in 1905 was the first by an Asian power over a European one in modern times.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war">Russo-Japanese War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1915">1915 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">111 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">'The Birth of a Nation' premieres in Los Angeles</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">D. W. Griffith's Civil War epic pioneered techniques of film storytelling but glorified the Ku Klux Klan. It drew protests from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naacp">NAACP</a> and helped inspire the Klan's revival that year.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1974">1974 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">52 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Skylab 4 crew return after 84 days in space</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Gerald Carr, Edward Gibson and William Pogue splashed down after the longest crewed mission yet. Their experience of long-duration flight informed later space stations.</p></div></li></ol>
